    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Speaking languages",
     "texto": [
      "**说** means «to speak». **中文** and **汉语** are two common ways to say «Chinese» as a language; **英语** means «English» and **西班牙语**, «Spanish». In English we don't put an article before a language name, and in Chinese there isn't one either."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A short question",
     "texto": [
      "**哪儿** and **哪里** mean «where». **住** means «to live» and **学习**, «to study» or «to learn». To answer, repeat the information: **你住哪儿？—我住在西班牙。**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
